From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Sinyavin <sinyavin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rtl8192es: preserve the primary full-MAC wdev

Reject deletion of the persistent primary interface to avoid recursively
entering cfg80211 while its wiphy mutex is held.

Signed-off-by: Dmitry Sinyavin <sinyavin@gmail.com>
---
--- a/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
@@ -4903,6 +4903,20 @@ static int cfg80211_rtw_del_virtual_intf
 	if (ndev) {
 		adapter = (_adapter *)rtw_netdev_priv(ndev);
 		pwdev_priv = adapter_wdev_data(adapter);
+#ifdef CONFIG_RTW_MF283V_PRIMARY_WDEV
+		/*
+		 * The RTL8192ES firmware has one persistent primary full-MAC
+		 * interface.  del_virtual_intf() is called with the wiphy mutex
+		 * held; unregistering that netdev recursively enters cfg80211's
+		 * NETDEV_UNREGISTER notifier and deadlocks on the same mutex.
+		 * Userspace must bring this interface down and reuse it instead.
+		 */
+		if (is_primary_adapter(adapter)) {
+			RTW_WARN(FUNC_NDEV_FMT" refusing to delete primary wdev\n", FUNC_NDEV_ARG(ndev));
+			ret = -EOPNOTSUPP;
+			goto exit;
+		}
+#endif
 
 		if (ndev == pwdev_priv->pmon_ndev) {
 			unregister_netdevice(ndev);
